                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "c9e379d9-1d03-4abd-90a2-f4eb44a3cf1e",
                        "source_entry_id": "0501349c-b73d-3749-9820-9b0ec736be1d",
                        "source_sense_id": "b75c62b6-93b4-305c-b982-26f8d7a2682a",
                        "source_sense_description": "Canis aureus, hondachtig roofdier",
                        "target_lang_word": "Schakal",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Schakal",
                                "target_lang_code": "de",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e382cfb0-e174-331a-bd5b-87cc2e7fa531",
                                        "entry_id": "fef6c4d2-1acd-36fd-ba81-866efc0bc1f8",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Wildhund, der von wolfsähnlicher Gestalt, aber deutlich kleiner ist und Afrika und Asien vorkommt"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "df08d627-3ace-4ce3-8bf1-bf1216621aa7",
                                                "sense_id": "e382cfb0-e174-331a-bd5b-87cc2e7fa531",
                                                "text": "Der ägyptische Gott Anubis wurde mit dem Kopf eines Schakals dargestellt."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "66d9c253-7947-45d4-a900-6f8d37c3801f",
                                                "sense_id": "e382cfb0-e174-331a-bd5b-87cc2e7fa531",
                                                "text": "„Ein Schakal frisst keinen Schakal.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "48ce0abe-f3b7-4321-a908-90877d15193b",
                                                "sense_id": "e382cfb0-e174-331a-bd5b-87cc2e7fa531",
                                                "text": "„Es handelt sich um den Hals und Kopf eines Schakals, Inkarnation des Gottes Anubis, der über die Einbalsamierung und die Seelen wacht.“"
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "c87158d9-826a-4f82-ae78-0a863cec4135",
                        "source_entry_id": "0501349c-b73d-3749-9820-9b0ec736be1d",
                        "source_sense_id": "b75c62b6-93b4-305c-b982-26f8d7a2682a",
                        "source_sense_description": "Canis aureus, hondachtig roofdier",
                        "target_lang_word": "jackal",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "jackal",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4667fb23-5905-3fc0-afc2-23d5589460d5",
                                        "entry_id": "acc1ab67-5e23-3023-a3ed-526c556eb2c5",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Any of certain wild canids of the genera Lupulella and Canis, native to the tropical Old World and smaller than a wolf."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1d6abf32-08cf-4d96-a04a-83e4ad2e7e8a",
                                                "sense_id": "4667fb23-5905-3fc0-afc2-23d5589460d5",
                                                "text": "In passing, it also mentions how the jackal and the tiger acquired their reddish spots. All of the animals referred to, except the deer, have tricksterlike personalities, both in this tale and in other story contexts. But the jackal is the most renowned of all for roguishness."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "59d2451f-945e-4a1f-8534-b69f9c802407",
                                                "sense_id": "4667fb23-5905-3fc0-afc2-23d5589460d5",
                                                "text": "Until recently, scientists thought Ethiopian wolves were a type of jackal. They gave Ethiopian wolves names like Semien jackal, Simenian jackal, or Ethiopian jackal."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0158c5b4-1765-4b60-a993-81a2ad595ed8",
                                                "sense_id": "4667fb23-5905-3fc0-afc2-23d5589460d5",
                                                "text": "As we will see, the jackal is usually associated in the Indic context with death and impurity, and would therefore sit squarely at the bottom of Dumont's social hierarchy."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "44066c0a-6bcd-3023-8b55-f7046593a545",
                                        "entry_id": "acc1ab67-5e23-3023-a3ed-526c556eb2c5",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A person who performs menial or routine tasks; a dogsbody."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d967fc0e-fa87-449d-a9a9-6a2fecb753ae",
                                                "sense_id": "44066c0a-6bcd-3023-8b55-f7046593a545",
                                                "text": "A nephew of hers, after receiving some learning at her ladyship's expence, got a commission, and fell upon the field of Waterloo; another is still at her heels, as a sort of jackall to fetch and carry when required."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "06127e50-7a73-37ea-9cb5-7373afbdcb02",
                                        "entry_id": "acc1ab67-5e23-3023-a3ed-526c556eb2c5",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A person who behaves in an opportunistic way; especially a base collaborator."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "derogatory"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4c970f29-b9c2-3eb7-a533-932091c68393",
                                        "entry_id": "acc1ab67-5e23-3023-a3ed-526c556eb2c5",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A jack (the playing card)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "rare",
                                            "slang"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "30c89feb-74bf-3a4b-856c-4c0c55404b89",
                                        "entry_id": "acc1ab67-5e23-3023-a3ed-526c556eb2c5",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A player who steals the ball at the tackle."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "jackal",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "524848d3-79a7-3659-96f5-2c9403bf1dfa",
                                        "entry_id": "f10a95b1-b0c9-36d6-9cad-fd3f92bfca83",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To perform menial or routine tasks"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e679c214-3e60-4965-a842-0e566314826a",
                                                "sense_id": "524848d3-79a7-3659-96f5-2c9403bf1dfa",
                                                "text": "They have jackalled for the great beast, to pick in turns the bones of each other; they have subserved those above, to oppress and defraud those below; and they are suffering, and, so far as classes can, justly suffering their purgation."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "ff8f19be-b04d-4d8e-82db-d2d114ab9a23",
                        "source_entry_id": "0501349c-b73d-3749-9820-9b0ec736be1d",
                        "source_sense_id": "b75c62b6-93b4-305c-b982-26f8d7a2682a",
                        "source_sense_description": "Canis aureus, hondachtig roofdier",
                        "target_lang_word": "chacal",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "chacal",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "41593c39-c67f-3864-a9d2-9b0bd9c41170",
                                        "entry_id": "e074e17a-8321-37e2-b647-a977fd371419",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Canidé carnivore d’Afrique et d’Asie, de taille moyenne ou petite."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "79fde7ec-b337-4e6c-a3d6-3cd28825a57e",
                                                "sense_id": "41593c39-c67f-3864-a9d2-9b0bd9c41170",
                                                "text": "Car la région que nous traversons est assez giboyeuse, et les grands nemrods de la m'halla, […], qui ont emmené des meutes de lévriers et des faucons chasseurs, font des hécatombes de lièvres, de perdrix, de poules de Carthage, de renards et de chacals."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "384de118-0751-49c7-8dde-3e87f9fc9827",
                                                "sense_id": "41593c39-c67f-3864-a9d2-9b0bd9c41170",
                                                "text": "Au fond de la vallée de l’Oued Mia, un chacal aboie."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "99d9b7ef-845a-3663-90af-63e22870c3cb",
                                        "entry_id": "e074e17a-8321-37e2-b647-a977fd371419",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Personne sournoise et opportuniste."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "pejorative"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f8a082d4-42bf-4f6a-8b8c-33a86217aa96",
                                                "sense_id": "99d9b7ef-845a-3663-90af-63e22870c3cb",
                                                "text": "Tu ne sortiras pas, ô Roi ! de mes liens,\nEt je te châtirai dans ta chair et ta race,\nÔ vipère, ô chacal, fils et père de chiens !"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "127af880-b82f-4de1-b252-a2ee6a2e5906",
                                                "sense_id": "99d9b7ef-845a-3663-90af-63e22870c3cb",
                                                "text": "Butron était un sale petit chacal. Je ne m'en suis aperçu qu'après-coup, quand j'ai su quel rôle il avait joué dans l'affaire N'Gustro. C'était un vrai nazi. Un chacal. Un sale petit chacal."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ec20e1b5-7134-4f73-a606-e00303a532ab",
                                                "sense_id": "99d9b7ef-845a-3663-90af-63e22870c3cb",
                                                "text": "Quel chacal ce type !"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
